<<<
-FIED. The spelling of the jocular compounds in which a verb in -fy hardly exists is unsettled (countrified or countryfied &c.). It seems best to use -i- when the noun or adjectiv~ does not provide a convenient connecting syllable, but, when it does, not to alter it; so cockneyfied, countryfied, dandyfied, Frenchified, ladyfied, townified, yankeefied.
===
**-FIED.** The spelling of the jocular compounds in which a verb in *-fy* hardly exists is unsettled (*countrified* or *countryfied* &c.). It seems best to use *-i-* when the noun or adjective does not provide a convenient connecting syllable, but, when it does, not to alter it; so *cockneyfied, countryfied, dandyfied, Frenchified, ladyfied, townified, yankeefied*.
>>>

